{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Before He had made the earth and the open areas</b> — like the Targum [meaning] 'before.' עשה [is] like [in] 'I, YHWH, have made.' וחוצות are the markets. And the meaning: upon the ground suitable for settlement." "<b>And the head</b> — [in] the sense of 'before.' So too: 'I was appointed from of old, from ראש' [Proverbs 8:23]." "<b>The dusts of the world</b> — as if it said 'and before the dusts of the world.' That is the settled world, and it is a doubling of meaning in different words."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:34.747701324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}